", "rxn_003", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_004", "mol_012"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "Hydrothermal CO2 \u2192 pyruvate \u2192 alanine (pyridoxal/metal-aided transamination)", "description": "Pyruvate, formed hydrothermally, is aminated via pyridoxal and Fe(III)/Al(III) catalysis to alanine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_010", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_004", "mol_012"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Hydrothermal CO2 \u2192 pyruvate \u2192 alanine (Bucherer\u2013Bergs with cyanide input)", "description": "Hydrothermal pyruvate reacts with surface-supplied cyanide, ammonia, and CO2 in the Bucherer\u2013Bergs pathway.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_004", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_004", "mol_012"]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Strecker-cyanide photoredox cascade (HCN photoreduction + Strecker)", "description": "HCN is photoreduced to acetaldehyde (cyanosulfidic), which enters classical Strecker synthesis with HCN and ammonia.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_007", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_006", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Surface Strecker from primordial aldehyde atmospheres", "description": "Preformed acetaldehyde (from atmospheric photolysis or discharge) reacts in Strecker sequence to form alanine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_010", "mol_012"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Bucherer\u2013Bergs: surface-supplied pyruvate or imported pyruvate (parent body)", "description": "Pyruvate accumulates by other means (HCN homologation, delivery, or CO2 surface fixation) and undergoes Bucherer\u2013Bergs synthesis.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_004", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_013", "mol_012"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Formose\u2013thiol route (Weber) from formaldehyde, glycolaldehyde, ammonia, thiol", "description": "C1/C2 feedstocks assembled to sugars, aminated by thiol-catalyzed condensation t