erature but is penalized for major mass conservation violations.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_003\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Balance all reactions; add H2O or CO2 where required.\",\n        \"Provide explicit coefficients and check all reactants/products for accurate formulas.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.6,\n        \"rxn_012\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.60,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.90,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n      \"target_achievement\": 1.0,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.75,\n      \"feedback\": \"Hydrothermal transamination from pyruvate is plausible and experimentally supported (notably when pyridoxal and metal ions are present), but rxn_001 and rxn_010 reactions are not balanced. Otherwise, the logical steps and environmental assignments are robust. Chiral amplification step is correctly included.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Balance reaction equations and check for missing byproducts.\",\n        \"Clarify pyridoxal/metal cofactor requirements if claimed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_012\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.70,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.90,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n      \"target_achievement\": 1.0,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.80,\n      \"feedback\": \"The Bucherer\u2013Bergs route from pyruvate is fully described in recent literature and does support prebiotic alanine synthesis. Rxn_004 is balanceable, but rxn_001 is still C, H, O unbalanced, so minor penalty. Surface/aqueous conditions align with experiment. Both logic and convergence with